-- title:
--   Translation and fibres of the level-ℓ Čerednik–Drinfeld family
-- statement:
--   The statement concerns the formal uniformisation, at an auxiliary prime $\ell$, of the fine moduli space of fake elliptic curves with full level $n$ and an extra $\ell$-level structure. Its hypotheses fall into the following groups; each group is named, and in several cases its many clauses are summarised here.
--
--   **Arithmetic data.** Primes $r$, $\bar r$ and a natural number $N$ with $\bar r\neq r$ (`hrr`), $r\nmid N$ (`hrN`), $\bar r\nmid N$ (`hrbarN`), and $N$ squarefree (`hN`).
--
--   **Coefficients (`hdvr`, `hπ`, `hcomplete`, `hres`, `hunr`).** A characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal O$ which is a discrete valuation ring, an irreducible element $\pi$, completeness of $\mathcal O$ for the ideal $(\pi)$, $\#(\mathcal O/\pi)=r$, and $(r)=(\pi)$; a characteristic-zero fraction field $K_0$ of $\mathcal O$.
--
--   **Unramified layer (`hOnr_complete`, `hOnr_max`, `hOnr_alg`, `hOnr_closed`, `hFr`).** A characteristic-zero domain $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ over $\mathcal O$ with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $Fr$, complete for the ideal generated by $\pi$, that ideal being maximal, every element of $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ satisfying some monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo $\pi$, every monic polynomial over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ of positive degree having a root modulo $\pi$, and $Fr(x)\equiv x^{r}\pmod\pi$. A homomorphism $vdet\colon \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)\to\mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) with $vdet(g)=n$ exactly when $\det g=u\,\pi^{n}$ for some $u\in\mathcal O^{\times}$ (`hvdet`).
--
--   **Indefinite side and moduli (`hB`, `hΛ`, `h𝒳`, `hn`, `hrn`, `hrbarn`, `hnN`, `hM`, `hρ`, `hp`, `hρp`, `hp_pt`).** Rationals $a,b$ with $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ indefinite and ramified exactly at $\{r,\bar r\}$, a maximal order $\Lambda$, a coarse moduli scheme $\mathcal X\to\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with point map `pt` for fake elliptic curves of level $N$, an integer $n\ge 3$ prime to $r$, $\bar r$ and $N$, a fine moduli scheme $M\to\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with point map `ptF` for full level $n$, a group $G$ acting by automorphisms $\rho$ of $M$ with labels $\chi\colon G\to\Lambda$ realising the level-twist action, and a morphism $p\colon M\to\mathcal X$ over the base which is $G$-invariant and compatible with the point maps.
--
--   **Hecke tower and Atkin–Lehner data (`h𝒴`, `hd₀f`, `hd₁f`, `hd₀`, `hd₁`, `harf`, `harbarf`, `har`, `harbar`).** For each prime $\ell'$ different from $r,\bar r$ a coarse moduli scheme $\mathcal Y(\ell')$ with extra $\ell'$-level, two degeneracy maps $d_0,d_1$ over the base which on points forget the extra level, respectively pass to an $\ell'$-isogenous quotient, and endomorphisms $a_r$, $a_{\bar r}$ of $\mathcal X$ over the base realising the Atkin–Lehner quotients at $r$ and $\bar r$ on points.
--
--   **Definite side (`hdef`, `hΛ₁`, `hR₁`, `hRΛ₁`, `hn₁`, `hS₁`, `hι₀`, `hv`).** Rationals $a_1,b_1$ with $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ definite and ramified exactly at $\bar r$, a maximal order $\Lambda_1$, an Eichler order $R_1$ of level $N$ contained in it, an adelic unit $n_1$ in the $r$-th prime Hecke set of $R_1$ with $\mathrm{meetOrder}(R_1,n_1)$ Eichler of level $N r$, an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra map $\iota_0\colon\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]\to M_2(K_0)$, and a height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ containing $r$.
--
--   **Groups and Hecke elements (`hΓt`, `hs`, `hΓtℓ`, `hwbar`).** $\Gamma^{t}$ is the group of units which are integral away from $v$ for $R_1$; for each prime $\ell'\neq r,\bar r$ elements $s(\ell')$ and adelic units $sf(\ell')$ with: $sf(\ell')$ equal to $s(\ell')\otimes 1$ at every finite place not containing $r$, equal to $1$ at the places containing $r$, the product of the diagonal image of the scalar $\ell'$ with $sf(\ell')^{-1}$ lying in `levelHeckeUSet Λ₁ (meetOrder R₁ n₁) ℓ'` when $\ell'\mid N$ and in `primeHeckeSet (meetOrder R₁ n₁) ℓ'` otherwise, and $\mathrm{nrd}(s(\ell'))=\ell'$; $\Gamma^{t}_{\ell'}=\Gamma^{t}\cap s(\ell')\Gamma^{t}s(\ell')^{-1}$; and a unit $\bar w$ of reduced norm $\bar r$ normalising $\Gamma^{t}$.
--
--   **The special fibre object (`hΛℤ`, `hcoord`, `hX₀`, `hA₀`, `he`).** Integers lie in $\Lambda$; a coordinate map $\mathrm{coord}\colon\Lambda\to \mathrm{Zp2}(r)^{2}$ which is additive, unital, multiplicative in the Frobenius-twisted sense, injective, of dense image and trace-compatible; a fake elliptic curve $A_0$ over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/\pi$, a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X_0$ of height $4$, formal coordinates $\theta_0$ of dimension $2$ presenting $A_0$ through $\mathrm{coord}$, endomorphisms $e(\gamma),e'(\gamma)$ of $A_0$ over the base indexed by $\Gamma^{t}$, and degrees $\deg$.
--
--   **Action package (`hE1`, `hE1mul`, `hE1sc`, `hE1'`, `hE2`, `hE3`, `hE4`).** Each pair $(e(\gamma),e'(\gamma))$ is an isogeny pair of degree $r^{\deg\gamma}$ preserving the $N$-level; multiplicativity of $\gamma\mapsto e(\gamma)$ up to multiplication by powers of $r$; rational scalars act, up to $r$-powers, by the corresponding integer multiplication, and conversely only scalars do; a formal comparison identifying, for every injective $E_0$ on the centraliser of the $X_0$-action and $\varpi$, the endomorphism induced on $\theta_0$ by $e(\gamma)$ with $r^{k_\gamma}\,g\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g^{-1}$; a labelling $\Gamma^t\to\Lambda$ describing the effect of $e(\gamma)$ on a full level-$n$ structure, multiplicative and scalar-compatible modulo $n$; and the surjectivity statement that over an algebraically closed field every $r$-power isogeny of a pullback of $A_0$ preserving the level comes from some $\gamma\in\Gamma^t$ up to $r$-powers.
--
--   **Order actions (`hR₂`, `hR₂o`, `hR₂r`, `hê`, `hE5a`, `hE5b1`, `hE5b2`, `hE5b3`, `hE5c`, `hE5d`, `hE5e`, `hE5g`; `hΛ₁s`, `hR₁Λ₁s`, `htwin`, `hR₂'`, `hR₂'o`, `hR₂'r`, `hR₂R₂'`, `hê'`, `hE6a`, `hE6b1`, `hE6b2`, `hE6b3`, `hE6c`, `hE6d`, `hE6e1`, `hE6e2`, `hE6f`).** Orders $R_2\le R_1$ and $R_2'\le \Lambda_{1s}$, with $\Lambda_{1s}$ a second maximal order such that $\Lambda_1\cap\Lambda_{1s}=R_1$, each $r$-power dense in the ambient order and $R_2\le R_2'$, together with actions $\hat e$, $\hat e'$ by endomorphisms of $A_0$ over the base which are additive on points, commute with $\Lambda$, preserve the level, are unital and multiplicative, send integers to integer multiplications, satisfy $\hat e(\bar x)\circ\hat e(x)=[\mathrm{nrd}\,x]$, are compatible with $e(\gamma)$ on $r$-power multiples of $\gamma$ and with $\hat e$ on $R_2$, are star-stable, faithful, admit the same formal comparison with $\iota_0$ as above, and satisfy the $q$-torsion criterion `hE6f` for primes $q\neq r$.
--
--   **Special formal moduli (`hΦ`, `hΦ4`, `hMD`, `hη`, `hE₀`, `hκ`, `hβ₀`).** A ring map $\iota\colon\mathrm{Zp2}(r)\to O^{\mathrm{nr}}$, a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $\Phi$ over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/r$ which is special for $\iota$ and of height $4$, a moduli package $MD$ satisfying the Zariski sheaf condition, a map $\eta$ from rigidified objects to $MD$-points whose three clauses give: the isomorphism criterion for admissible rigidifications over Noetherian bases, naturality, and local surjectivity; an injective $E_0$ on the centraliser of the $\Phi$-action with $\pi$-power-bounded image in $M_2(\mathcal O)$; a residue map $\kappa$ compatible with the two quotient maps; and an isogeny $\beta_0$ from $\Phi$ to $X_0$ base-changed along $\kappa$, of height $4n_0$.
--
--   **Drinfeld comparison (`hnatD`, `hbijD`, `hfstD`, `hGLD`, `hPiD`, `hPiexD`).** A natural bijection $eD$, on Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebras with $\pi$ nilpotent, between the $MD$-point functor and the product of $B\mapsto(O^{\mathrm{nr}}\to_{\mathcal O}B)$ with the Deligne datum functor $\Omega$, whose first component is the structure map, which transports the $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$-action to the twisted action on $\Omega$, sends $\pi$-translation to the Frobenius twist, and for which $\pi$-translates always exist.
--
--   **Rigidification comparison (`hΞleg`, `hΞnat`, `hΞiso`, `hΞdef`) and equivariance (`heqΓ`, `heqW`, `heqS`).** A map $\Xi$ sending rigidified fake elliptic curves over Noetherian $\pi$-nilpotent $\mathcal O$-algebras to $MD$-points, whose leg over a connected base is an integral Frobenius twist of $\psi$, which is natural under pullback, invariant under isomorphisms admitting a comparison of rigidification data up to $r$-power multiplications, and computed by transport of rigidified special formal modules with $j\le 1$; and, for a fixed $g_0\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$, three dictionaries stating that translating a rigidification by $e(\gamma)$, by an Atkin–Lehner $\bar r$-quotient, and by an $\ell'$-level isogeny corresponds under $\Xi$ to the action of $r^{c}\,g_0\iota_0(\gamma)g_0^{-1}$, of $r^{c}\,g_0\iota_0(\bar w)g_0^{-1}$, and of $r^{c}\,g_0\iota_0(\ell'\,s^{-1})g_0^{-1}$ respectively, the last subject to the same local conditions on $s,sf$ and to the joint formal comparison for $\iota_0(\bar s)$.
--
--   **Atkin–Lehner and level-$\ell'$ objects over the special fibre (`hALw`, `hBSw`, `hBSwlev`, `hJOINTw`; `hLIs`, `hBSs`, `hBSslev`, `hJOINTs`, `hSTAB`).** A curve $A_{0w}$ with maps $a_w,a_w'$ realising the Atkin–Lehner $\bar r$-quotient of $A_0$ and an $r^{k_w}$-isogeny pair $b_w,b_w'$ back to $A_0$ preserving the level, with a joint formal comparison matching $a_w\circ b_w$ to $\bar w$; for every prime $\ell'\neq r,\bar r$ an extra $\ell'$-level $C_0(\ell')$ on $A_0$, a curve $A_{0s}(\ell')$ with the corresponding level isogeny and an $r^{k_s}$-isogeny pair back, with a joint formal comparison matching the composite to $\overline{s(\ell')}$; and the stabiliser dictionary `hSTAB`: $e(\gamma)$ preserves factorisation through $C_0(\ell')$ exactly when $\gamma\in\Gamma^{t}_{\ell'}$.
--
--   **Level-$n$ uniformisation (`θt`, `hnat`, `hG`, `hi'`, `het`, `hfib`, `hC0e`, `hC0u`, `hC1e`, `hC1u`, `hC1p`, `hC2`, `hC2c`, `hC3`, `hC4`, `hC4pi`, `hC5`).** A homomorphism $\theta^{t}\colon\Gamma^{t}\to G$ and a map $\Theta_f$ from triples (an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $O^{\mathrm{nr}}\to B$, a Deligne datum over $B$, an element of $G$) to $B$-points of $M$ over $\mathcal O$, which is natural, equivariant for $\rho$, satisfies the translation property for $\gamma\in\Gamma^{t}$ and the fibre description over algebraically closed fields, has the unique-lifting property along surjections whose kernel squares to zero, and the clauses `hC0e`–`hC5` giving: existence and uniqueness of the normalised full level, existence, uniqueness and pullback of rigidified curves matching a prescribed Deligne datum, the two value clauses identifying $\Theta_f((\psi,P),1)$ with the `ptF`-point of $(E,P_n)$ and its image in $\mathcal X$ with the `pt`-point of $E$, the transport of rigidifications along the twisted action of $\gamma$ and of an arbitrary unit together with the induced twist of the full level by $\chi(\theta^t\gamma)$ and the comparison of extra levels, the $\pi$-translation clause, and the recognition clause `hC5` over algebraically closed fields.
--
--   **Extra-level bookkeeping and coarse tower uniformisation (`hCLe`, `hCLu`, `hnatT`, `hVT`).** Existence and uniqueness, up to the factorisation relation, of an extra $\ell'$-level on $E$ transported along a rigidification from a given extra level on $A_0$; and a natural map $\Theta_T(\ell')$ to $B$-points of $\mathcal Y(\ell')$ whose value at $(\psi,P)$ is the `ptT`-point of $(E,C)$ under the matching conditions.
--
--   **The level-$\ell$ data.** For a fixed prime $\ell\neq r,\bar r$: a fine moduli scheme $M_\ell\to\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ for full level $n$ together with an extra $\ell$-level, with point map `ptFℓ` (`hMℓ`); a forgetful morphism $\pi_\ell\colon M_\ell\to M$ over the base compatible with the point maps (`hπℓf`, `hπℓ`); a morphism $p_\ell\colon M_\ell\to\mathcal Y(\ell)$ over the base compatible with the point maps (`hpℓg`, `hpℓ`); an action $\rho_\ell$ of $G$ on $M_\ell$ over the base, commuting with $\pi_\ell$ and $p_\ell$ in the stated sense and satisfying the twisting law `hρℓtw` for $\chi(h)$-twists matching the extra levels; and a map $\Theta_{f,\ell}$ from triples as above, defined on Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebras with $\pi$ nilpotent, to $B$-points of $M_\ell$ over $\mathcal O$, which is natural (`hnatℓ`), satisfies $\rho_\ell(h)\circ\Theta_{f,\ell}(x,g h)=\Theta_{f,\ell}(x,g)$ (`hGℓ`), and satisfies the value clause `hVALℓ`: whenever the leg of $\Xi$ is the prescribed Frobenius twist, the twisted-action relation to $(\psi,P)$ holds, $P_n$ is the normalised level transport of $P_0$ and $C$ corresponds to $C_0(\ell)$, the point $\Theta_{f,\ell}((\psi,P),1)$ equals the `ptFℓ`-point of $(E,P_n,C)$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Two assertions about $\Theta_{f,\ell}$ hold.
--
--   (i) (Translation.) For every Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ in which the image of $\pi$ is nilpotent, every unit $\gamma$ of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ lying in $\Gamma^{t}$ and in $\Gamma^{t}_{\ell}$, every pair $x,x'$ consisting of an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $O^{\mathrm{nr}}\to B$ together with a Deligne datum over $B$, and every $g\in G$: if $x'$ arises from $x$ by the twisted action of $\iota_0(\gamma)$ — that is, the first component of $x'$ is the first component of $x$ precomposed with $Fr^{-vdet(\iota_0\gamma)}$, and the Deligne datum of $x'$ is the pullback of that of $x$ along $\iota_0(\gamma)^{-1}$, meaning that for every full lattice $M$ the line of $x'$ at $M$ is the preimage of the line of $x$ at $\iota_0(\gamma)^{-1}M$ under the base-changed lattice isomorphism — then
--   $$\Theta_{f,\ell}\bigl(x',\ \theta^{t}(\gamma)\,g\bigr)=\Theta_{f,\ell}\bigl(x,\ g\bigr).$$
--
--   (ii) (Fibres.) For every algebraically closed field $k$ which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra in which the image of $\pi$ is nilpotent, all $\mathcal O$-algebra maps $\psi,\psi'\colon O^{\mathrm{nr}}\to k$, all Deligne data $P,P'$ over $k$ and all $g,g'\in G$, the equality $\Theta_{f,\ell}((\psi,P),g)=\Theta_{f,\ell}((\psi',P'),g')$ holds if and only if there exists a unit $\gamma\in\Gamma^{t}$ such that: $\gamma\in\Gamma^{t}_{\ell}$; $g'=\theta^{t}(\gamma)\,g$; $P'$ is the pullback of $P$ along $\iota_0(\gamma)^{-1}$ in the above sense; and for every $y\in O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ which is fixed by $Fr^{\,vdet(\iota_0 z)}$ for every $z\in\Gamma^{t}$ that is a rational scalar and satisfies $\theta^{t}(z)=1$, one has $\psi'(y)=\psi\bigl(Fr^{-vdet(\iota_0\gamma)}y\bigr)$.
--
--   Thus (i) is the analogue for $\Theta_{f,\ell}$ of the translation clause `hi'` for $\Theta_f$, with the additional requirement $\gamma\in\Gamma^{t}_{\ell}$, and (ii) is the analogue of the fibre clause `hfib`, with the additional conjunct $\gamma\in\Gamma^{t}_{\ell}$ on the right-hand side of the equivalence.
--
--   These are the translation and fibre clauses of the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation of the Shimura curve tower, carried from full level $n$ to the tower with an extra $\ell$-level structure: the uniformising map $\Theta_{f,\ell}$ is invariant under translation by those $\gamma\in\Gamma^{t}$ which stabilise the chosen $\ell$-level, and its geometric fibres are exactly the orbits of that subgroup. The result feeds the construction of the level-$\ell$ lift of the tower family, [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.IsFineModuli.exists_fineFamilyT_lift_of_towerFamily_of_isNoetherianRing_heightNormalised_eq_oneLegC5`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.IsFineModuli.exists_fineFamilyT_lift_of_towerFamily_of_isNoetherianRing_heightNormalised_eq_oneLegC5).
